  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-14, in chat): \"in Geometry of an operation - its not possible to pick two edges with Ctrl+<LMB> - that should result in an open selection, where the edges act as boundaries with oppen ens that the pass can get extended within, thus not \"going around a corner\" like it does when choosing a face..\"\n\nWhat happens: on the Geometry tab of an operation, Ctrl + left mouse button on a second edge does not add that edge to the selection. The user cannot pick two edges together.\n\nExpected:\n- Ctrl + left mouse button adds each picked edge to the geometry selection of the operation.\n- Two picked edges that do not make a closed loop give an open selection. The edges are the boundaries of the cut.\n- The ends of an open selection are open ends. The pass can extend past them.\n- The pass does not go around a corner at an open end. A face pick gives a closed boundary, and the pass follows it around the corners.\n\nNot yet known: the operation kind and the model in the report, and whether the pick is refused or replaces the first edge. The worker must read the pick code and reproduce the case with a UI test before the fix.\n\nSafety: a change to the cut region changes the toolpath. The gouge check must judge the extended pass.\n\nDone means: a UI test pins that Ctrl + left mouse button on two edges selects the two edges; a toolpath test pins that the open selection gives a pass that stays between the edges, extends at the open ends and does not turn the corner; the selection change is an undoable command and the MCP tool `set_operation_geometry` accepts the same open selection.\n",
